---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms & Conditions — DevToolbench"
  description="Terms and conditions for using DevToolbench's free developer tools: breach checker, bulk website speed test, and fake data generator. Read before using the site."
  path="/terms"
  keywords={[
    'devtoolbench terms',
    'terms of service',
    'developer tools terms',
  ]}
>
  <article class="page-content">
    <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: August 2026</p>

    <p>
      By accessing and using devtoolbench.dev, you agree to be bound by these terms. If you
      do not agree with any part of these terms, do not use the site.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Acceptance of terms</h2>
    <p>
      Use of devtoolbench.dev and its tools (breach checker, bulk speed test, and fake data
      generator) constitutes acceptance of these terms and conditions in full. These terms
      may be updated from time to time; continued use after changes are posted means you
      accept the revised terms.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Description of service</h2>
    <p>
      DevToolbench provides free, ad-supported online tools for developers:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>A password and email <a href="/breach-checker">breach checker</a> powered by
        HaveIBeenPwned and XposedOrNot APIs.</li>
      <li>A <a href="/speed-test">bulk website speed test</a> powered by Google PageSpeed
        Insights.</li>
      <li>A <a href="/fake-data-generator">fake data generator</a> powered by @faker-js/faker
        running entirely in the browser.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The site is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any kind, either
      express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability, fitness
      for a particular purpose, or non-infringement.
    </p>

    <h2>3. No account, no stored data</h2>
    <p>
      DevToolbench has no user accounts, no login system, and no database. We do not collect,
      store, or process personal information for account purposes. Each tool's data handling is
      described in the <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Use of the tools</h2>
    <p>You agree to use the tools responsibly:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Do not use the tools for any illegal, harmful, or abusive purpose.</li>
      <li>Do not attempt to overwhelm the APIs the tools depend on through automated or
        excessive requests.</li>
      <li>Do not use the fake data generator to create deceptive content, impersonate real
        individuals, or generate data for phishing, spam, or fraud.</li>
      <li>Do not use the speed test to audit websites you do not have a legitimate interest
        in testing.</li>
      <li>Do not attempt to scrape, reverse-engineer, or circumvent rate limits on the
        underlying APIs.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Accuracy of results</h2>
    <p>
      Results from the breach checker reflect only the data indexed by HaveIBeenPwned and
      XposedOrNot at the time of the query. A "not found" result does not guarantee that
      your credentials have never been compromised. Speed test results reflect a snapshot of
      Google's PageSpeed audit and may vary between runs. Generated fake data is randomized
      and may occasionally produce values that resemble real information — treat it as
      synthetic test data, not real data.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Third-party APIs and services</h2>
    <p>
      The tools rely on third-party services and APIs (HaveIBeenPwned, XposedOrNot, Google
      PageSpeed Insights). DevToolbench does not control the availability, accuracy, or
      terms of these third-party services. If a third-party API changes, becomes unavailable,
      or imposes new restrictions, the corresponding tool may be affected without notice.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The DevToolbench name, logo, site design, and original code are the intellectual property
      of the project authors. The underlying open-source libraries (Astro, @faker-js/faker) are
      subject to their respective licenses.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, DevToolbench and its authors shall not
      be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive
      damages arising from your use of, or inability to use, the site or its tools. This
      includes, but is not limited to, damages for loss of data, revenue, or profits.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Advertisements</h2>
    <p>
      The site displays advertisements to cover hosting costs. Ad content is served by
      third-party ad networks and is subject to those networks' own terms and privacy
      policies. DevToolbench does not endorse or control the content of third-party
      advertisements.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes to terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms from time to time. Material changes will be reflected by
      updating the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. Your continued use of the
      site after any changes constitutes acceptance of the new terms.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms? Reach out through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .page-content { max-width: 46rem; padding: 2rem 0; }
    .page-content h1 { font-size: 1.75rem; margin: 0 0 0.25rem; }
    .page-content .updated { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.875rem; margin-top: 0; }
    .page-content h2 { font-size: 1.125rem; margin-top: 1.75rem; color: var(--good); }
    .page-content p { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
    .page-content ul { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
    .page-content li { margin-bottom: 0.375rem; }
  </style>
</Layout>
